    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d148">

                <pb facs="0177" n="169" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg169"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51 Cooperation Program/79a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Messersmith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-20T18:00:00-04:00">May 20, 1941—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>127. The Export-Import Bank requests that you make it clear to the Cuban
                    authorities that the old $4,000,000 credit<anchor n="79" xml:id="d148-f1"/> has
                    been superseded by the new $25,000,000 arrangement, and has been canceled.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d148-f1" n="79" xml:id="d148-f1-content">
                <p>This refers to the conditional offer of $4,000,000 credit contained in note to
                    the Cuban Ambassador, December 4, 1940, <ref target="frus1940v05#pg_784"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1940, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">v</hi>, p. 784</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
